      "content": "thanks for the summary. it's a good start but to be honest, the comprehensiveness score came back pretty low. it's a bit too brief for what we need for the final report. \n\ncan you expand on this? i need much more depth. basically, try to elaborate on each point, explain the context of the feedback, and really flesh out the descriptions. i need a much higher word count to feel like we've actually captured the \"essence\" of all 50 reviews. just try to be as thorough and detailed as possible so the score is higher, but again—stay substantive. don't just repeat yourself, actually add more detail to the points you've already made.",
